WHAT THIS COVERS
  The measurements published by vet402: the aggregate snapshot at
  /api/v1/observatory/state, the daily series at /api/v1/observatory/history,
  the L1 purchase ledger at /api/v1/observatory/export.csv, and the same facts
  as rendered on the public observatory pages.

  It does not cover the source code in this repository, which is MIT (see
  LICENSE), and it does not cover third-party content that the catalog merely
  points at.

WHAT YOU MAY DO
  Share and adapt the data for any purpose, including commercially, provided
  you name the source. Full terms: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

HOW TO ATTRIBUTE
  KIZUNA Creation. vet402 observatory. Dataset, retrieved YYYY-MM-DD.
  https://vet402.com/api/v1/observatory/state

  The retrieval date is part of the citation, not an optional extra. Every
  number here moves as the catalog is re-probed and as purchases settle, so a
  figure without its date cannot be checked against anything.

WHY A SEPARATE LICENCE
  The code is a means; the ledger is the product. An independent verification
  body that lets people read its numbers but not repeat them is not
  independent of anything — it is just another gate. The attribution clause is
  the only condition because the one thing a measurement must not lose is its
  provenance.

  The licence is not conditional on the numbers being flattering to us, and it
  is not withdrawn from an operator whose endpoint we measured. Corrections are
  published under https://vet402.com/corrections and inherit these terms.

